<title>USA: UAL's United Air, IBM in marketing pact.</title>
<headline>UAL's United Air, IBM in marketing pact.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>UAL Corp's United Airlines said Monday it reached an agreement with International Business Machines Corp and Speedwing International, a British Airways Plc subsidiary, to market United's E-Ticket service to airlines worldwide.</p>
<p>The agreement designates IBM as implementor of choice for United's E-Ticket (electronic ticketing) product.</p>
<p>IBM will install and support electronic ticketing systems for airline customers based on United's products. Speedwing was granted exclusive marketing rights for many of its customers.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
